                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "69148412",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198125156883",
                            "num_reviews": 15,
                            "playtime_forever": 261,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 226,
                            "last_played": 1589512033
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Waste of money even at $4 on sale. Missions don't give enough information at the start to allow you to know if you want (or even can) complete them. E.g. I accepted a gladiator challenge, and only after that found I don't have the ships needed. Instant fail. Or enemy suddenly produces a mega-weapon and wipes me out even though he is outnumbered 3-1. When your flagship dies it is game over, so rinse and repeat ... except the map is different every time so you can never learn from your mistakes. \n\nNote that no-one who has reviewed this game in the last 3 years has even played 10h - that should give you a warning...",
                        "timestamp_created": 1589504351,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1589504351,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 13,
                        "votes_funny": 1,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6634633541107178,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "I'm sorry the game hasn't lived up to your expectations, but I'm hoping I can address some of your concerns and make the game as fun as possible. My design goal for the Rogue Fleet campaign was to make a challenging experience similar to games such as \"FTL\" focusing on learning boss mechanics and ideal fleet compositions over multiple plathrough attempts. All of the boss super abilities can be avoided with experience, and campaigns can be saved before any mission to reload. Additionally, failed campaign attempts boost the player's starting fleet on the next new campaign, and lost flagships are already replaced with the base model any time the player enters a new campaign zone. In any case, that was my thinking on the campaign design, it might be that this isn't something that appeals to everyone, but I hope I can continue to make the game more fun for more players.\n\nWe've just released a new patch that should address some of the more difficult or more unforgiving missions in the campaign.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1589574019,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
